# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LinkedIn Skills for OpenCode — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to:  ~/.config/opencode/skills/linkedin/.env
# All variables are OPTIONAL.
# Skills work in draft-only (Tier 0) mode with nothing set.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── TIER 1 — Publora auto-post (recommended) ─────────────────────
# Sign up free: https://app.publora.com/signup
# 15 LinkedIn posts/month on free tier
PUBLORA_API_KEY=sk_your_key_here

# LinkedIn platform connection ID (format: linkedin-ABC123)
# Found in: Publora dashboard → Channels → your LinkedIn account
LINKEDIN_PLATFORM_ID=linkedin-your_id_here

# ── Apify — Read layer (optional) ────────────────────────────────
# Fetches post bodies, comments, thread data, and engager lists.
# Free tier: $5/month credit (~1,000 post fetches or ~1,000 comment fetches).
# Sign up:  https://console.apify.com/sign-up
# Token:    https://console.apify.com/settings/integrations
# Without this, skills ask you to paste content manually.
APIFY_TOKEN=apify_api_your_token_here

# ── Pixfaro — Image layer (optional) ─────────────────────────────
# Generates post illustrations, carousel slides, and quote-cards.
# The image URL flows directly into Publora's media_urls on publish.
# Sign up: https://api.pixfaro.com/signup?ref=linkedin-skills
# Key format: pf_live_...
# Without this, skills draft the image prompt for you to generate manually.
PIXFARO_TOKEN=pf_live_your_token_here

# ── TIER 2 — Custom poster (advanced) ────────────────────────────
# If you've built your own LinkedIn poster (Playwright, official API, etc.),
# set this to the command the skills should invoke on approval.
# Leave unset unless you actually have a working custom poster.
# LINKEDIN_SKILLS_CUSTOM_POSTER=python /path/to/my-poster.py
